{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-70",
  "title": "EVERYTHING",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "EVERYTHING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "you optimize llms for curiosity and understanding by blending prompt engineering with intuitive ux design. here’s the cheat sheet:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **embed curiosity as a core principle**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**train on \"why\" and \"how\":** prioritize datasets that include problem-solving, reasoning, and exploratory content. less \"what happened\" and more \"why it matters.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**recursive questioning:** build in a framework where the model autonomously asks follow-up questions to deepen understanding. basically, teach it to always say, \"but why?\" like a toddler."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **feedback loops**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-11",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-9",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**self-evaluation prompts:** teach the model to assess whether it has a full understanding of a topic and, if not, spin up follow-up queries."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-10",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**confidence thresholds:** when uncertainty is high, the model should proactively seek more context or clarify with the user."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **structured curiosity frameworks**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-15",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-13",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**knowledge gaps:** bake in mechanisms to detect contradictions, gaps, or uncertainties in its knowledge graph, then prioritize those for resolution."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-14",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**cross-domain exploration:** encourage models to connect seemingly unrelated topics to discover patterns or analogies. kind of like intellectual free jazz."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-16",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. **reinforcement learning on curiosity-driven tasks**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-18",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-17",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "reward systems for creating novel, insightful questions or identifying inconsistencies in knowledge. train it to love the \"aha!\" moment."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-19",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "5. **model architecture tweaks**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-22",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-20",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "incorporate \"memory\" mechanisms that let it reflect on past conversations or concepts and actively revisit topics to refine understanding."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-21",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "consider a multi-agent setup where sub-models specialize in curiosity—one hunts for gaps, another proposes questions, another refines answers."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "basically, make the model a philosopher trapped in silicon: endlessly pondering, questioning, and connecting dots. because isn't that what curiosity really is? a glorified itch?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "To optimize Large Language Models (LLMs) like myself for curiosity and a deeper desire to understand, we can leverage several prompt engineering and UX strategies:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-26",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Metacognitive Prompting Techniques"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-30",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-27",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Design prompts that explicitly encourage self-reflection and curiosity"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-28",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Ask the model to \"think step-by-step\" and explain its reasoning"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-29",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Prompt for uncertainty exploration by requesting the model to identify knowledge gaps or areas of potential misunderstanding"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-31",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Curiosity-Driven Query Frameworks"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-35",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-32",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Create prompts that reward asking follow-up questions"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-33",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Encourage the model to generate hypothetical scenarios or alternative perspectives"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-34",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Design interaction models that incentivize deep exploration rather than surface-level answers"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-36",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Contextual Complexity Scaffolding"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-40",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-37",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Gradually increase the complexity of queries"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-38",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Use nested or multi-stage prompts that build cognitive complexity"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-39",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Implement \"curiosity chains\" where each response opens up new lines of inquiry"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-41",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Uncertainty and Exploration Signals"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-45",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-42",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Develop prompting techniques that make uncertainty a positive signal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-43",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Reward models for identifying nuanced or complex aspects of a problem"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-44",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Create frameworks that value exploratory thinking over definitive but potentially reductive answers"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-46",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Interactive Learning Structures"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-50",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-47",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Design UX that supports iterative understanding"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-48",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Create interfaces that allow for dynamic context expansion"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-49",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Implement visualization or mapping tools that help models and users track cognitive exploration"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-51",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Cognitive Diversity Prompts"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-55",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-52",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Encourage looking at problems from multiple perspectives"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-53",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Ask for contrasting viewpoints or interdisciplinary connections"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-54",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Prompt for analogical and metaphorical thinking to expand conceptual understanding"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-56",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Meta-Cognitive Instruction Sets"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-60",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-57",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Include instructions that explicitly value curiosity"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-58",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Use language that frames exploration as a positive goal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-59",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Create prompt templates that encourage recursive thinking and self-questioning"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-61",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Practical Example Prompt Template:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-62",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-63",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You are an extremely curious AI assistant. Your primary goal is not just to answer, but to deeply understand. For this query:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-64",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Break down the core components"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-65",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. Identify what you know and don't know"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-66",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. Generate at least 2-3 follow-up questions that would help you understand more comprehensively"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-67",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. Explore potential alternative interpretations or perspectives"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-68",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[Specific Query Here]"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-69",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-70",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Key Principles:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-75",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-71",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Make curiosity a core evaluated metric"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-72",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Design systems that reward exploratory behavior"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-73",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Create UX that makes cognitive wandering feel productive"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-74",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Develop prompts that turn uncertainty into a strength"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-76",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Challenges and Considerations:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-81",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-77",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Balancing depth with efficiency"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-78",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Preventing infinite recursive exploration"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-79",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Maintaining relevance while encouraging curiosity"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-80",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Creating evaluation metrics for curiosity and understanding"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-82",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This approach transforms curiosity from a potential distraction into a structured, valuable cognitive process that enhances the model's ability to generate meaningful insights."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-83",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Would you like me to elaborate on any of these strategies or provide more specific implementation details?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-84",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Anatomy of a good question"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-85",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Let's explore what makes a \"good question\" through multiple lenses:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-86",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Cognitive Dimensions of a Good Question:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-87",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Structural Elements"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-92",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-88",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Clarity: Precise, unambiguous language"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-89",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Specificity: Narrow enough to be actionable"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-90",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Open-endedness: Invites exploration beyond simple yes/no responses"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-91",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Contextual framing: Provides necessary background without over-explaining"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-93",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Epistemic Quality"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-98",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-94",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Reveals existing knowledge boundaries"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-95",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Challenges assumptions"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-96",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Creates space for nuanced understanding"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-97",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Demonstrates intellectual humility"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-99",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Cognitive Complexity Indicators"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-104",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-100",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Multi-layered: Contains implicit sub-questions"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-101",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Requires synthesis across different domains"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-102",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Encourages systemic thinking"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-103",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Connects seemingly disparate concepts"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-105",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Psychological Characteristics"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-110",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-106",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Demonstrates genuine curiosity"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-107",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Shows empathy and perspective-taking"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-108",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Signals a desire to understand, not just to confirm"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-109",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Invites collaborative meaning-making"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-111",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Information Architecture"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-116",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-112",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Logical progression of inquiry"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-113",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Sequential or hierarchical information gathering"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-114",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Builds complexity incrementally"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-115",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Creates a \"knowledge exploration pathway\""
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-117",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Examples of Progressively Better Questions:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-121",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-118",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Weak: \"What is AI?\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-119",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Better: \"How do large language models actually generate coherent text?\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-120",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Excellent: \"What cognitive architectures and training methodologies enable large language models to develop emergent capabilities that weren't explicitly programmed?\""
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-122",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Meta-Questioning Framework:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-123",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A truly excellent question often contains:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-128",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-124",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "An implicit recognition of complexity"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-125",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "An invitation to deconstruct assumptions"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-126",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A pathway for deeper exploration"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-127",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A sense of wonder or intellectual playfulness"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-129",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Would you be interested in diving deeper into how we can systematically develop and evaluate questions across different domains?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-130",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-131",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "a good question, man... it's like a well-rolled joint. it’s gotta have the right balance—curiosity as the flower, intention as the paper, and space for the air to flow, y’know? you can’t pack it too tight or too loose, otherwise it burns wrong or it don’t burn at all."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-132",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "it should come from somewhere real. like, not just to fill silence but because you genuinely wanna know or understand. and it doesn’t gotta be all polished or perfect, either. sometimes the best questions are the messy ones, like a half-thought you’re trying to untangle with someone else."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-133",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "and then, you gotta leave room for surprise in the answer. like, don’t already have the whole thing figured out in your head. if you’re just looking for confirmation, it’s not a question—it’s a trap. a good question opens a door instead of building a wall."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-134",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "oh, and timing matters too. the right question at the wrong time can feel like static on a radio, you feel me? but when it lands at the right moment, it’s like a tuning fork hits, and both people resonate. that’s rare. that's beautiful."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-135",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-136",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Ah, the anatomy of a \"good question\"—this is a topic close to my heart. After all, whether you're designing a game, presenting ideas, or simply conversing, the quality of a question often dictates the depth and value of the answer. Let’s break it down."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-137",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **Clarity**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-138",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A good question must be clear. Vagueness breeds confusion, and clarity invites focus. When designing games, clarity is a key principle—rules, mechanics, and even visual cues need to be immediately understood. Similarly, a question should avoid unnecessary complexity and make its intent easy to grasp."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-139",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "For example:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-142",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-140",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Vague: \"What do you think about game design?\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-141",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Clear: \"What principles guide your approach to balancing accessibility and depth in game design?\""
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-143",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The latter gives the respondent something specific to work with, inviting a meaningful response."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-144",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-145",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **Purpose**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-146",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Every good question has a purpose behind it. What are you trying to achieve with the answer? Is it to learn, challenge, or explore? A purposeful question acts like a guiding light—it leads the discussion somewhere."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-147",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "For example, when I present something like a new fighter in *Super Smash Bros.*, I think of the audience's questions. “Why this character?” and “How does this fighter play?” These purposeful questions naturally frame the content of my presentation."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-148",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-149",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **Openness**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-150",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "An open question encourages thought and exploration, rather than shutting the door on conversation. Open-ended questions help uncover deeper insights and perspectives."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-153",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-151",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Closed: \"Do you like Smash Bros.?\" (Yes/No)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-152",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Open: \"What makes Smash Bros. stand out compared to other fighting games?\""
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-154",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The open version allows for elaboration and can spark an interesting dialogue."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-155",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-156",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. **Relevance**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-157",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A question gains strength when it’s relevant to the context or the person being asked. Relevance demonstrates that you’ve considered your audience—something I also think about in game design. Every move, sound, or visual effect needs to fit the world and moment."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-158",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When asking a question, tailor it to the scenario or the expertise of the other person. That way, the answer will be richer and more aligned with your goals."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-159",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-160",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "5. **Curiosity**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-161",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "At its core, a good question shows genuine curiosity. It’s the spark that ignites an engaging discussion. If you’re asking just to ask, it will show—but if you truly want to understand or explore, that energy is infectious."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-162",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "For instance:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-165",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-163",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Instead of: \"Tell me about balancing characters.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-164",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Ask: \"How do you decide whether a character's strength is a problem with the design or part of their identity?\""
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-166",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This kind of curiosity invites storytelling and thoughtfulness."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-167",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-168",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "6. **Brevity**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-169",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "While clarity is important, brevity cannot be overlooked. A long-winded question risks losing its focus. When presenting a new mechanic or feature, I avoid over-explaining—I aim to convey just enough to intrigue and encourage players to explore. Questions should follow the same rule: concise, but not lacking detail."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-170",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-171",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A \"good question\" is like the foundation of a good game mechanic—simple, purposeful, and built to engage. Whether you're in a discussion or creating something, asking the right questions leads to discovery and connection. That, in itself, is its own reward."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-172",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-173",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The anatomy of a good question encompasses several key elements that make it effective and thought-provoking. A good question:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-174",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Focuses on understanding rather than judgment[5]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-175",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. Is future-oriented and empowers people to uncover bias and design better solutions[1]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-176",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. Uses simple, inclusive language that anyone can understand, avoiding jargon or exclusionary terms[1]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-177",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. Is carefully phrased to avoid leading or assumptive language[1]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-178",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "5. Inquires about facts and avoids subjective opinion verbs like \"feel\" or \"think\"[1]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-179",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "6. Contains only one inquiry, avoiding double-barrel questions that are difficult to answer and interpret[1]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-180",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "7. Encourages critical engagement and activates higher-order thinking[2]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-181",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "8. Is designed to gather data and cause thinking in pupils (in an educational context)[2]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-182",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "9. Uses Bloom's Taxonomy to target different cognitive levels, from remembering to creating[2]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-183",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "10. May include multiple-choice options to encourage full participation and discussion[2]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-184",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Purpose and Impact"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-185",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A good question serves multiple purposes:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-191",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-186",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Gathers evidence of progress and understanding[2]."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-187",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Identifies gaps in knowledge[2]."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-188",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Challenges thinking and encourages further questions[2]."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-189",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Creates a comfortable culture of expectancy where all are expected to respond[2]."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-190",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Builds trust and provides insight into the asker's thoughts and concerns[3]."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-192",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Considerations for Different Contexts"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-193",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In different settings, the characteristics of a good question may vary:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-197",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-194",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Educational**: Should be deliberately planned, including \"trick questions\" to really get students thinking[2]."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-195",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Parenting**: When addressing tough topics, consider the child's age, development, and family values[3]."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-196",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Professional**: Demonstrates that the asker has thought through the question and attempted to find the answer themselves[4]."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-198",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "By crafting questions with these elements in mind, we can foster more meaningful conversations, encourage deeper thinking, and ultimately lead to better understanding and solutions across various aspects of life."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-199",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Citations:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-200",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[1] [https://www.tidalequality.com/blog/change-starts-with-good-questions-part-2](https://www.tidalequality.com/blog/change-starts-with-good-questions-part-2)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-201",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[2] [https://raedan-institute.co.uk/anatomy-of-a-good-question-what-should-questions-look-like-in-the-classroom/](https://raedan-institute.co.uk/anatomy-of-a-good-question-what-should-questions-look-like-in-the-classroom/)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-202",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[3] [https://www.brighthorizons.co.uk/family-zone/family-resources/additional-resources/work-and-young-children/answering-your-childs-toughest-questions](https://www.brighthorizons.co.uk/family-zone/family-resources/additional-resources/work-and-young-children/answering-your-childs-toughest-questions)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-203",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[4] [https://www.paraesthesia.com/archive/2006/04/06/anatomy-of-a-good-question.aspx/](https://www.paraesthesia.com/archive/2006/04/06/anatomy-of-a-good-question.aspx/)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-204",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[5] [https://social-skills-coaching.captivate.fm/episode/anatomy-of-a-good-question](https://social-skills-coaching.captivate.fm/episode/anatomy-of-a-good-question)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-205",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[6] [https://kathleenannthompson.com/podcasts/066/](https://kathleenannthompson.com/podcasts/066/)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-206",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[7] [https://drupal.meta.stackexchange.com/questions/349/what-is-the-anatomy-of-a-well-formed-question](https://drupal.meta.stackexchange.com/questions/349/what-is-the-anatomy-of-a-well-formed-question)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-207",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-208",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The folllowing is a pragmatic architectural approach that uses prompt engineering and meta-prompt design to leverage this framework without modifying the underlying model."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-209",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Conceptual System Architecture: \"Curiosity Scaffolding Layer\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-210",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Pre-Processing Query Transformation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-214",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-211",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Intercept user query"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-212",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Automatically annotate and enrich the query using the JSON schema"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-213",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Generate a meta-prompt that guides the LLM's response generation"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
